Terraform:
===========
Terraform is an open-source Infrastructure as Code (IaC) tool created by HashiCorp. 
Its purpose is to let you build, change, and manage cloud and on-premises computing resources safely and efficiently 
using human-readable configuration files instead of manual user interfaces.

1) Install Terraform:
=======================
For Linux
CentOS/RHEL
sudo yum install -y yum-utils
sudo yum-config-manager --add-repo https://rpm.releases.hashicorp.com/RHEL/hashicorp.repo
sudo yum -y install terraform

References:
https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/install#linux


2) Terraform File Structure and Organization:
===============================================
Terraform common files:
A) main.tf  
 > primary infrastructure components 

B) Variables.tf 
 > Variable definitions used through your infrastructure
 
C) Outputs.tf 
 > Show output value to your console
 
D) providers.tf 
 > providers configuration and requirements 
 
E) terraform.tfvars 
> assigns concrete values to the input variables declared in your Terraform configuration

Additional Terraform files:
  terraform.tfstate 
 > the file that terraform uses to store state / to keep track your current state of your infrastructure
 
 terraform.tfstate.backup 
  > backup the previous state file before terraform writes anything new to the state file

 .terraform.lock.hcl  
 > used to track and select provider version and consistency
 
3) Terraform State:
======================
Enables terraform to determine the difference between desired and current state.
It also uses for dependency management and code collaboration.


